{"id":"longest-substring-without-repeating-characters","title":"Longest Substring Without Repeating Characters","difficulty":"Medium","pattern":"Sliding Window","tags":["Hash Table","String","Sliding Window"],"companies":{"google":3,"apple":3,"meta":3,"amazon":5,"microsoft":4},"description":"Given a string `s`, return the length of the longest **contiguous** substring in which no character appears more than once.","examples":[{"input":"s = \"abcabcbb\"","output":"3","explanation":"`abc` is the longest such substring."},{"input":"s = \"bbbbb\"","output":"1"},{"input":"s = \"pwwkew\"","output":"3","explanation":"`wke` works; `pwke` is a subsequence, not a substring."}],"constraints":["0 <= s.length <= 5 * 10^4","s consists of ASCII characters (letters, digits, symbols, spaces)."],"hints":["Expand a window to the right one character at a time. When does the window become invalid?","Keep the set of characters in the window. When the new character is already in it, shrink from the left until it is gone.","Faster: store each character's last index. If the repeat is inside the current window, jump the left edge to just past that index instead of shrinking one step at a time."],"function":"lengthOfLongestSubstring","signature":"def lengthOfLongestSubstring(self, s: str) -> int:","arg_types":{"s":"str"},"return_type":"int","compare":"exact","tests":[{"input":{"s":"abcabcbb"},"output":3},{"input":{"s":"bbbbb"},"output":1},{"input":{"s":"pwwkew"},"output":3},{"input":{"s":""},"output":0},{"input":{"s":"a"},"output":1},{"input":{"s":"abba"},"output":2},{"input":{"s":"dvdf"},"output":3},{"input":{"s":"tmmzuxt"},"output":5},{"input":{"s":" "},"output":1},{"input":{"s":""},"output":26},{"input":{"s":""},"output":10}],"solution":"class Solution:\n    def lengthOfLongestSubstring(self, s: str) -> int:\n        last_seen = {}\n        left = 0\n        best = 0\n        for right, ch in enumerate(s):\n            if ch in last_seen and last_seen[ch] >= left:\n                left = last_seen[ch] + 1\n            last_seen[ch] = right\n            best = max(best, right - left + 1)\n        return best\n","approach":"**Sliding window with last-seen indices.** Maintain a window `[left, right]` that contains no repeats. When the character at `right` was last seen at an index inside the window, move `left` to one past that index; otherwise the window simply grows. Record the character's new position and update the best length.\n\n**Why it works:** the window is always the longest duplicate-free substring ending at `right`, because `left` is placed just after the nearest earlier occurrence of any character in the window. Every substring is considered implicitly through its right endpoint.\n\n**Common mistakes:** setting `left = last_seen[ch] + 1` without checking `last_seen[ch] >= left` (then `left` can move backwards on input like `abba`, which is exactly what the `abba -> 2` test catches); using a set and shrinking one step at a time is correct but you should know the jump version; treating the problem as 'distinct characters' rather than 'contiguous substring'.\n\n**Interview follow-ups:** Return the substring itself (remember the best `left`). Longest substring with at most k distinct characters (count map, shrink while `len(map) > k`). Longest substring with at most k repeats allowed per character.","complexity":{"time":"O(n)","space":"O(min(n, alphabet))"},"similar":["longest-repeating-character-replacement","minimum-window-substring","permutation-in-string"],"number":26,"starter":"class Solution:\n    def lengthOfLongestSubstring(self, s: str) -> int:\n        pass\n"}